  "sourceNotes": "Cold sesame noodles appear across northern and Sichuan Chinese cooking under various names including ma jiang mian (sesame paste noodles). The dish is documented in Chinese culinary literature throughout the twentieth century and gained wide international recognition through Chinese-American restaurants from the 1970s onward. The base formula is consistent across regional Chinese cookbooks: sesame paste, soy, vinegar and chilli combined with cold boiled noodles.",
