    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This is one of those dishes that takes about 20 minutes and serves 4 generously. Wheat noodles are boiled, rinsed cold, then tossed in a dressing built on"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "tahini",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "tahini"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", soy sauce, rice vinegar and"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "chilli oil",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "chilli-oil"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". A splash of"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Shaoxing wine",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "shaoxing-wine"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "and a drizzle of"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "sesame oil",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "sesame-oil"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "round out the flavour."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Rinse the cooked noodles under cold running water immediately after draining and toss with a little oil to keep them from clumping. This step makes a real difference to the texture."
          }
        ]
      },
